<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105118" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρι-πάχυιος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παχύς</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>thrice-fattened, thrice-gorged,</i> epith. of
			the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίμων</span> of the Atridae (perh. in
			allusion to the <i>three</i> visitations mentioned in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				1065
			</span></i>-<i><span class="en">
				74
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1476
			</span></i> (lyr.):—the word is doubtful; Bamberger proposed
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριπάχυντον,</span> referring to <i><span class="en">
				<u>Th.</u>
				771
			</span></i>; Blomf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριπάλαιον;</span>
			Bamberger (olim) <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριπαλαιστήν.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
